Hello!

I'm just asking myself if I'm seriously missing something. My Valkyrie 
(AC -44, +6 Mjollnir, foo-resistant) got to Ghennom without any great 
problems and tends to survive about everything that gets thrown at her.

And yet, in Ghennom, she is perishing.

It is a painful, slow death, but one I can't see her escaping.

She is dying of boredom.

I mean, really, am I missing something, or is Ghennom really so 
monotoneous? It's like run through _all_ the screen, curse, look under 
every stupid piece of loot that's lying around, curse some more, finally 
find the stair, go down, rinse, repeat. Is there _anything_ to make this 
place even remotely interesting?

I can remember playing nethack (uh... most likely it was hack back then, 
or even rouge?) about ten years ago, and then there was only one level 
of labyrinth, at 24 or so, where you found the amulet. What on earth got 
the dev team to extend it to the now 20 levels of mazes my Valkyrie has 
seen so far?

Ok, it's a whining post, but this is really frustrating: The game was 
fun until right after the castle, getting the char up, looking forward 
to getting the amulet, perhaps seeing the planes... And now I'm not able 
to play for more than 10 minutes without giving up, disencouraged by the 
ever-repeating pure boredom that hits me in Ghennom :(


